    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Central African kingdom south of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">Mbanza Kongo</a> by an elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikongo">manikongo</a>.</li><li>It was among the first African states to sustain diplomacy with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, adopting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and Portuguese literacy.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> fuelled rivalries, and defeat at Mbwila in 1665 tipped it into civil war and long decline.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Kongo used nzimbu shells, gathered on the royal fishery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda-island">Luanda Island</a>, as currency alongside squares of finely woven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raffia-cloth">raffia cloth</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

